                <pb facs="0240" n="132" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg132"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-02-17"><hi rendition="#italic">February 17, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 173.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit copy and
                    translation of correspondence between the senior commanders of the foreign naval
                    forces, the diplomatic representatives whose governments are represented by
                    naval forces, and the minister of foreign affairs, with the view of securing a
                    safer anchorage for the war and merchant vessels lying in the harbor.</p>
                <p>It has been pleasant to observe the willingness and promptness with which his
                    excellency the Vice-President has responded to every request of the
                    commanders.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. L.
                    Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>











